<title>FRANCE: German rye went for 88.60 Ecus, $103 a tonne.</title>
<headline>German rye went for 88.60 Ecus, $103 a tonne.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The EU sold a small quantity of German intervention rye on Thursday at 88.60 Ecus per tonne, officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The price, for a volume of 9,218 tonnes, was in line with the previous sale from German intervention and was worth around $103 per tonne on the world market, they said.</p>
<p>Some reports had put the price lower at 68.60 Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
